From cd76a072588ac0b0ba12e93614a482e63c5f5c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuxi Luo <yl5960@columbia.edu>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:24:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(equity): ground text sections in labelled evidence,
 add a verifier

The text sections routinely presented reported results as forecasts or
"guidance", attached the historical CAGR to forecast years and cited
consensus that the data does not contain (2/3 of contradicted claims in
an audit of five reports). The causes are in the evidence, not only the
model: the prompt has no date, so the model writes from its training
cutoff, and forecast columns were hard-coded 2025E-2027E regardless of
the latest reported year.

- Label forecast years from the base year (FY+1..FY+3). The
  --revenue-growth-2025/2026/2027 flags keep their names and apply to
  FY+1..FY+3. Escape % in their help strings (--help used to crash).
- Start every writer prompt with reading notes: report date, which
  columns are reported and which are the pipeline's forecast (with its
  assumptions), the CAGR period, the projected peer year, and that the
  data has no guidance, consensus or news. annotate=False reproduces
  the old prompt.
- Add modules/claim_verifier.py and --enable-verifier (default model
  gpt-4.1-mini): after each section is written it is checked against the
  writer's data; sentences that mislabel reported vs forecast figures,
  misattribute the CAGR period, misquote numbers or cite non-existent
  sources are replaced by exact-sentence corrections, logged in
  verifier_log.json. Statements the data does not cover are listed,
  not deleted. On any verifier error the text is left unchanged.
- Stop replacing valid takeaways with canned text: the check required
  the exact string "Revenue Growth:" and the model writes
  "**Revenue Growth**", so every takeaways section was discarded.
